* CABSRT11 - BILL DETAIL SORT FOR THE JURISDICTIONAL SUMMARY
* SORTS THE VARIABLE LENGTH BILL DETAIL BY OCN / STATE /
* JURISDICTION SO THAT CABRPT02 CAN BE RUN WITHOUT ITS INTERNAL
* MATRIX WHEN THE MATRIX OVERFLOWS.  THE ORDER MATTERS BECAUSE
* THE REPORT WALKS THE FILE ONCE AND BREAKS ON EACH OF THE THREE
* FIELDS IN TURN.  THE POSITIONS ARE COUNTED FROM THE RDW.
*
* THIS SORT TAKES SORT, RECORD, MODS AND END AND NOTHING ELSE.
* THE EQUALS SETTING AND THE SHORT KEY TOLERANCE THAT THE DFSORT
* CARD CARRIED ARE BOTH GONE.  SHORT RECORD HANDLING IS NOW HELD
* IN E15 EXIT CABSXJUR, WHICH DELETES ANYTHING UNDER 108 BYTES
* RATHER THAN LET THE SORT TAKE A KEY OUT OF A TRUNCATED RECORD.
* CABSXJUR ALSO RE-DERIVES THE JURISDICTION BYTE FROM THE STATE
* AND LATA WHEN IT IS BLANK ON THE RECORD.
* NEITHER RULE IS VISIBLE ON THIS CARD.
 SORT FIELDS=(26,4,CH,A,31,2,CH,A,30,1,CH,A)
 RECORD TYPE=V,LENGTH=(1651,,,108,1651)
 MODS E15=(CABSXJUR,2048,SORTEXIT,N)
 END
